= Introduction

Establishing Downlink. . .

Welcome to Telemetry Troubles!

You begin your career with one of the Outer Rim League companies. There are many ways you can apply your talent within the League, but the fact that you are holding this playbook right now suggests you are considering a path in spacecraft systems engineering. Congratulations! A perfect choice!

But this is just the beginning of your troubles.
The following chapters cover the full depth of our deep-space exploration program and associated challenges. Are you ready to lead humanity into outer space?



== DUSTY-12

((DUSTY-12)) family of Command and Control Units is the latest series of spaceframes by the famous StarDust Bureau.


.Deep-Space Legacy
****
We all enjoy an abundance of memory and computational resources these days.
Home terminals use the Megabit satellite uplink to connect to powerful mainframes
of many Megahertz and Megabytes.
Even at home, many own workstations with up to 640Kb of RAM, which is more than enough
for any conceivable task.

So one might ask, why are our deep-space exploration vehicles so low-powered
and have very limited memory?

Partly it is explained by timing - it takes a lot of time to design and build a space probe and it takes many more years to reach the outer rim of the Solar System.
So the probes are limited by the technology available at the time of design and construction.

Also, we can't use stock components for the construction of such a probe. Strong magnetic fields, solar winds, flares, cosmic rays, and other high-energy phenomena are affecting the proper functions of electronic components. Therefore, all on-board computers are deliberately downgraded and made out of space-grade materials to harden them against such harsh conditions.

Indeed, DUSTY-12 looks peculiar, but there is a good reason for that weirdness.
****






